GATE EXECUTION NOTE (transparency — read before the results)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt's literal gate runs `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync[-macOS] build test`
against the in-repo project. Running that command verbatim from THIS prompt's scope
is not possible because of two integration facts that lie OUTSIDE this prompt's
allowed files (apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/TimeStamp.* + this log):

  1. apps/apple/project.yml registers source groups `TeslaSync/feature-views` and
     `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets`, but NOT `TeslaSync/shared-surfaces`. Until P4-core
     integration adds that one source path to the TeslaSync + TeslaSync-macOS targets,
     the repo project does not compile this surface. Editing project.yml is out of
     scope here (allowed files are TimeStamp.* + this log only).
  2. The repo scheme's pre-action builds Shared.xcframework (KMP/Kotlin-Native) via
     Scripts/build-shared-xcframework.sh. This surface is intentionally KMP-free (it
     imports no `Shared` symbols), so it does not need that framework.

To verify the surface HONESTLY with the real toolchain anyway, a standalone XcodeGen
harness was generated that compiles the EXACT shipped TimeStamp.* sources together
with the REAL design system (apps/design/generated/apple/Tokens.swift,
apps/apple/Sources/Design, apps/apple/Sources/Components/{UI,Motion},
.../Feedback/Skeletons.swift) — no stubs, no KMP — and runs the shipped XCTest files
on the iPhone 16 simulator (iOS) and on macOS. This is the same compiler, same SDKs,
same simulator the repo gate would use; only the project wrapper differs.

